      "jcr:created": "Thu Feb 19 2026 18:49:29 GMT+0000",
      "text": "You and your patients can now breathe easier. POM offers an innovative oxygen‑delivery solution for procedures requiring sedation. Contact us POM Procedural Oxygen Mask® Safety. Simplicity. Innovation. All in the same breath. A) Nose clip Secures the mask to the patient’s face. B) Oral & nasal membrane access ports Allows an instrument (scope, tube or probe) to enter either a patient’s oral or nasal passage. C) Oxygen adaptor port Allows for the insertion of a medium or high O2 concentration adaptor to facilitate oxygen delivery. D) Exhalation valve A one-way flap that allows the patient’s exhalation to vent or exit the mask. The valve closes during inhalation. E) EtCO2 sampling port with tethered cap Allows for the secure attachment of the EtCO2 sampling line to facilitate EtCO2 monitoring. F) Head strap Adjusts to accommodate appropriate size. Innovative oxygen delivery for procedures requiring sedation* Monitoring POM doesn’t just deliver oxygen to patients, it also samples gases for monitoring. POM helps decrease severe and prolonged hypoxic episodes and in-case interruptions, delays, and cancellations.**1 Versatile POM is a versatile multi-port oxygen mask, designed to accommodate a wide range of scopes, probes, and tubes with ease. With its unique design, it allows for hassle-free insertion through the patient’s mouth or nose, all while maintaining optimal oxygen delivery. POM is engineered to maximize oxygen flow and provide respiratory rate monitoring for enhanced safety. Sizes POM is now available in three sizes: large (adult), medium, and small (pediatric). For more information on the models available, see the resources section below for the full part number guide.",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Feb 19 2026 18:50:05 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/experienceFragment",
